# Virgil — User Configuration

> **Setup**: copy this file to `config/user.md` and replace bracketed placeholders with your own values.
> ```bash
> cp config/user.md.example config/user.md
> ```

**User**: [Your name]
**Created**: [YYYY-MM-DD]
**Last Updated**: [YYYY-MM-DD]

---

## Vault Location

The Obsidian vault (or any markdown folder) is the canonical data store. Virgil reads/writes here but does not own it.

**Path**: `[/absolute/path/to/your/vault/]`

Recommended folder structure inside the vault:

```
[vault]/
├── Scratch_Pad/          — inbox (unprocessed top, pending bottom)
├── Archive/              — labelled, processed notes
├── Daily Notes/          — YYYY-MM-DD.md (capture log → curated narrative)
├── Meetings/             — transcripts and meeting notes
├── Today.md              — daily to-dos
└── _notion_queue.md      — fallback queue for failed task-manager syncs
```

---

## Tools & Integrations

### Task Manager: Notion (default)

Virgil's default task manager is Notion. You can swap it for any task manager with an API (see `config/connectors.md.example`).

**Databases (FRAGILE — IDs break if the DB is moved or recreated)**

| Database | Data Source ID | DB ID (for curl) |
|---|---|---|
| Task Planner | `collection://[your-data-source-id]` | `[your-database-id]` |
| Goals & Projects | `collection://[your-data-source-id]` | |
| Weekly Sprints | `collection://[your-data-source-id]` | |
| Agent Updates | `collection://[your-data-source-id]` | `[your-database-id]` |
| Ideas (Raw Archive) | `collection://[your-data-source-id]` | |

Remove rows you don't use; add rows for additional DBs you do.

**How to find a Notion ID**: open the database in browser, copy the 32-character string from the URL.

### API Access Patterns

**Credentials**: Notion API token is in `.mcp.json` (gitignored). See `.mcp.json.example` for the format. Never hardcode tokens in skill files or any tracked config.

**Filtered database queries → direct curl (fastest)**:
```
curl -s -X POST 'https://api.notion.com/v1/databases/{db_id}/query' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer $NOTION_TOKEN' \
  -H 'Notion-Version: 2022-06-28' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"filter":{"property":"Status","select":{"equals":"Inbox"}}}'
```
- Use `"select"` (not `"status"`) for Status filter.

**Local Notion MCP** (`mcp__notion__`): `API-post-page`, `API-patch-page`, `API-post-search` work. `API-query-data-source` may be unreliable depending on server version — fall back to curl if it fails.

